# Instant Pot Stuffed Bell Peppers

Based on [https://www.wellplated.com/instant-pot-stuffed-peppers/…](https://www.wellplated.com/instant-pot-stuffed-peppers) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250801182444/https://www.wellplated.com/instant-pot-stuffed-peppers/)) and [ingredients from this Washington Post Recipe](https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/harissa-stuffed-bell-peppers/17096) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20220928002338/https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/harissa-stuffed-bell-peppers/17096))

{ rating="4" image="instant_pot_stuffed_bell_peppers.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 4 large [bell peppers]{ ing="bell-peppers" } (any color)
- [ ] (Optional) 1/2 lb [ground turkey]{ ing="ground-turkey" }, ground chicken, or lean ground beef
- [ ] 1 can (15 oz) [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" } (or Navy/Great Northern), rinsed
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [ground chili powder]{ ing="ground-chili-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [onion powder]{ ing="onion-powder" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" } (optional)
- [ ] 1 (10 oz) can Rotel diced tomatoes [and green chiles]{ ing="and-green-chiles" } (with juices)
- [ ] 1 (4 oz) can [diced green chiles]{ ing="diced-green-chiles" } in their juices
- [ ] 1.5 cups [cooked brown rice]{ ing="cooked-brown-rice" }, quinoa, etc.
- [ ] 1.25 cup [shredded cheese]{ ing="shredded-cheese" } (Monterey Jack, pepper jack, sharp cheddar, or similar), divided in 3/4 and 1/2 cup
- [ ] [Cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, salsa, non-fat plain yogurt, or other toppings

## Recipe

1. Pour 1 cup of water (1.5 cups for 8 qt) and place the trivet in the Instant Pot
1. Cut off the tops of the [peppers]{ ing="bell-peppers" }. Gently pull out the seeds and hollow out
1. Stand the [peppers]{ ing="bell-peppers" } up in the Instant Pot, nestling them beside each other so that they stay upright
1. In a large glass mixing bowl, place the ground meat and [beans]{ ing="black-beans" }

   1. Sprinkle on the [chili powder]{ ing="ground-chili-powder" }, [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, [garlic powder]{ ing="garlic-powder" }, [onion powder]{ ing="onion-powder" }, [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, and [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }

      1. Flip a few times to coat
   1. Pour in the cans of tomatoes/green chilies
   1. Add the [rice]{ ing="cooked-brown-rice" } and 3/4 cup [shredded cheese]{ ing="shredded-cheese" }
   1. Stir with a fork, but don’t overwork the meat
1. Using a spoon, scoop the filling into the [peppers]{ ing="bell-peppers" } until each is full to the top
1. Cook on high pressure for 10 minutes
1. Quick Release
1. Sprinkle the remaining 1/2 cup [cheese]{ ing="shredded-cheese" } on top of the [peppers]{ ing="bell-peppers" }
1. Replace the lid and let sit for the [cheese]{ ing="shredded-cheese" } to melt (~1 min)
1. With tongs, gently lift the [peppers]{ ing="bell-peppers" } onto serving plates
1. Serve hot, sprinkled with fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" } and any of your favorite toppings
